A||||4||Leadfoot||No fuel for you!!!||||8||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||06-29-2001||10:24 AM||||So I finally finished putting in my rebuilt engine.  I guesstimated the timing, filled the cooling system, purged the fuel system, and primed the oil system.  Check...check...and double check.  I start the puppy up this morning...it was noisy for the first 5 seconds but then quieted down.  (Good at least the lifters filled.)  The engine sounded like it wasn't firing on all cylinders so I shut it down and checked the wiring again. Yep! #4 wire wasn't connected all the way.  So I started the engine one more time and voila purred like a lion.  The r's were holding at 2000 but if I tapped the gas it would stumble (that's odd).  I figured since it is holding 2000 I would let it run for 20 minutes for a preliminary breakin.  I got out of the car to check for leaks and lone behold we have drippage.  At first I thought it was coolant but quickly found out it was fuel.  So I shut everything down again (not good).  Turns out the fuel return line connection at the fuel rail was leaking. (that explains the stumbling)  Since you can't tighten the lines without taking off the upper intake I decided to wait until the engine cooled before I started to take it apart.  When I took off the upper intake was I pissed.  Not only was the connection leaking it wasn't even connected.  Looks like the dumb a$$ (ME) who put the engine together stripped the aluminum threads off the fuel rail manifold. (stupid...stupid...stupid!).  So now I got to find a replacement, but who would have such an item available ASAP?  What really worries me though is that since I already shut the engine down twice during the 5 minutes it ran that the components didn't have a chance to wear-in properly.  Man! seems like this Friday the worlds a tuxedo and I'm a pair of brown shoes!  What do you guys think?    ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Oreif||06-29-2001||10:30 AM||||Well if you need it ASAP you can call Paul Vargyas or Archie. Archie probably has a few V-6's laying around. Like he says, "I have no uses for the V-6's or the 4's" So you may be able to get one quickly and not cost an arm and a leg. From here it's only a 20 minute ride to Archies.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Leadfoot||06-29-2001||10:33 AM||||Good idea! Thanks Oreif!||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||06-29-2001||11:45 AM||||The Fiero engine is the same as all of the W code 2.8L engines in the billions of Celebrities/Ciera/6000's in the junk yards. Also the S code engine in the Camaro Firebirds. Those fuel rails are the same and will work.||||reg||1
